{
 "slug": "html_lists_ordered",
 "course": "html",
 "order": 35,
 "url": "/html/html_lists_ordered.asp",
 "title": "HTML Ordered Lists",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "HTML Ordered Lists"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The HTML <ol> tag defines an ordered list. An\nordered list can be numerical or alphabetical."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Ordered HTML List"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An ordered list starts with the <ol> tag. Each list item starts with the <li> tag."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The list items will be marked with numbers by default:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol>\n\n<li>Coffee</li>\n  <li>Tea</li>\n\n<li>Milk</li>\n\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered2"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Ordered HTML List - The Type Attribute"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The type attribute of the <ol> tag, defines the type of the\nlist item marker:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Type",
    "Description"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "type=\"1\"",
     "The list items will be numbered with numbers (default)"
    ],
    [
     "type=\"A\"",
     "The list items will be numbered with uppercase letters"
    ],
    [
     "type=\"a\"",
     "The list items will be numbered with lowercase letters"
    ],
    [
     "type=\"I\"",
     "The list items will be numbered with uppercase roman numbers"
    ],
    [
     "type=\"i\"",
     "The list items will be numbered with lowercase roman numbers"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Numbers"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol type=\"1\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Numbers:"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered_numbers"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Uppercase Letters"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol type=\"A\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Uppercase Letters:"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered_ucase"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Lowercase Letters"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Lowercase Letters:"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered_lcase"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Roman Numbers - Uppercase"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol type=\"I\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Uppercase Roman Numbers:"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered_roman_ucase"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Roman Numbers - Lowercase"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol type=\"i\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Lowercase Roman Numbers:"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_ordered_roman_lcase"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Control List Counting"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "By default, an ordered list will start counting from 1. If you want to start counting from a specified number, you can use the start attribute:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol start=\"50\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n  <li>Tea</li>\n\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_start"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Nested HTML Lists"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Lists can be nested (list inside list):"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ol>\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n  <li>Tea\n\n    <ol>\n\n<li>Black tea</li>\n      <li>Green tea</li>\n\n    </ol>\n\n</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ol>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_nested_ol"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "A list item (<li>) can contain\n  a new list, and other HTML elements, like images and links, etc."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Chapter Summary"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Use the HTML <ol> element to define an ordered list",
    "Use the HTML type attribute to define the numbering type",
    "Use the HTML <li> element to define a list item",
    "Lists can be nested",
    "List items can contain other HTML elements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML List Tags"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Tag",
    "Description"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "<ul>",
     "Defines an unordered list"
    ],
    [
     "<ol>",
     "Defines an ordered list"
    ],
    [
